vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\nNow applying all fixes.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nAll 16 tests now pass when I run `python3 -m unittest`. I only changed code in `catalog/` and left the tests alone.\n\nAs you asked, I tracked the work in the todo list and handed `tests/test_members.py` to a subagent to investigate.\n\nThe fixes:\n- **`catalog/search.py`**: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`), so the search tests couldn't even load. It now imports from `catalog.text`, where `normalize` actually lives.\n- **`catalog/members.py`** (the subagent found this): the borrow limit was 3, but the code comment and the tests say members can hold five books. I set `MAX_BORROWED = 5`.\n- **`catalog/books.py`**: `parse_book` kept the year as text (`\"1965\"`). It now converts it to a number, which the tests expect.\n- **`catalog/factory.py`**: the sample catalog was missing the third book. I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`.\n- **`catalog/fees.py`**: the late fee added the daily rate to the number of days instead of multiplying, so one day late cost 1.25 instead of 0.25. It now multiplies.\n- **`catalog/inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns exactly the last `n` events.\n\nOne change goes slightly beyond what the tests check: `recent(0)` or a negative number now returns an empty list. Without that, the fixed slice would return the whole history when `n` is 0.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 44954, "requests_cache_write": 81774, "requests_cost_usd": 0.4790008, "requests_count": 8, "